Ladybird refreshes the connected FontFace after descriptor removal.
Blink’s AbstractPropertySetCSSStyleDeclaration::removeProperty() calls
DidMutate(), and StyleRuleCSSStyleDeclaration::DidMutate() notifies the
stylesheet. WebKit’s PropertySetCSSDescriptors::removeProperty() also
calls didMutate(). Gecko’s CSSFontFaceRuleDecl::RemoveProperty() resets
the descriptor through Servo_FontFaceRule_ResetDescriptor(), without a
matching update notification there. Ladybird keeps the connected face
synchronized with the rule.

Ladybird refreshes a connected face after cssText replacement, keeping
its identity when src is unchanged. Blink notifies the stylesheet in
StyleRuleCSSStyleDeclaration::DidMutate(), and Chrome updates rendering
but replaces the connected object. WebKit calls didMutate() from
PropertySetCSSDescriptors::setCssText(). Gecko rejects cssText changes
in CSSFontFaceRuleDecl::SetCssText(). Ladybird preserves its connection
semantics: A changed src disconnects the old face and creates another.

Ladybird resynchronizes a disconnected @font-face rule with its sheet
after descriptor edits. A valid, effective rule gets a fresh connected
FontFace; rules in inactive media or detached sheets stay disconnected.

Blink uses ScopedStyleResolver::AddFontFaceRules() to add connected
faces. FontFace::Create() rejects rules without font-family or src.
Chrome restores the face and its width for both edits.

WebKit propagates descriptor changes to the sheet from the method
PropertySetCSSDescriptors::didMutate(). Its font selector then removes
obsolete connections in CSSFontSelector::buildCompleted(), and passes
staged rules to addFontFaceRule(). That method checks the required
descriptors before it creates each face.

Gecko uses FontFaceSetDocumentImpl::UpdateRules() to reconcile faces.
Its InsertRuleFontFace() method rejects unusable family descriptors and
creates missing faces. CSSFontFaceRuleDecl::SetCssText() rejects block
replacement, so that CSSOM entry point differs. Ladybird follows Chrome
for both descriptor-edit paths.
